            <ArticleTitle>Hydatid cyst of the abdominal aorta and common iliac arteries complicated by a false aneurysm: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>637-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The rupture of hydatid cysts into the abdominal aorta is an unusual and serious complication of the hydatid disease. The authors describe a case of a 12-year-old girl with hydatid disease presenting as a retroperitoneal mass invading the wall of the abdominal aortic bifurcation and complicated by a false aneurysm. Difficulties of preoperative diagnosis and operative management were discussed, and the literature was reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
